{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XB5Fc24f95viWKyvdsHDxZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"validate-pair-rail-verdict.py — PLAN-081 Phase 6 release.yml step 15.\n3\t\n4\tValidates a Pair-Rail verdict artifact (`.claude/governance/\n5\tpair-rail-verdict-<release-tag>.md`) per R1 S-Sec-3 replay defense +\n6\tR1 S-Sec-4 inputs_hash determinism + R1 C5 Codex CLI pin enforcement\n7\t+ R1 S-QA-Unseen-2 distinct VERDICT_EXPIRED exit code.\n8\t\n9\t## Usage\n10\t\n11\t    python3 .github/scripts/validate-pair-rail-verdict.py \\\\\n12\t      --verdict-file .claude/governance/pair-rail-verdict-${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md \\\\\n13\t      --parent-sha ${PARENT_SHA} \\\\\n14\t      --release-tag ${GITHUB_REF_NAME} \\\\\n15\t      --max-age-hours 24 \\\\\n16\t      --recompute-inputs-hash \\\\\n17\t      --codex-cli-pin-file .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt \\\\\n18\t      --codex-pin-manifest-file .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin-manifest.json \\\\\n19\t      --inputs-hash-paths-file .claude/governance/pair-rail-inputs-hash-manifest.txt\n20\t\n21\t## ADR-182 payload pin (PLAN-163 T5.2)\n22\t\n23\t`--codex-pin-manifest-file` enforces the payload pin: the verdict\n24\tenvelope MUST declare `tool_versions.codex_target_triple` (the platform\n25\ttriple of the run that generated the verdict) and\n26\t`tool_versions.codex_payload_sha256` (sha256 of the NATIVE codex\n27\tpayload for that triple — NOT the npm JS launcher). The validator\n28\tcompares the declared sha against\n29\t`manifest.payloads[<triple>].sha256`. Fail-CLOSED: missing fields,\n30\ttriple absent from the manifest, malformed entry, or sha mismatch →\n31\tVERDICT_INVALID (3). Manifest file unreadable → infra (1). The legacy\n32\t`--codex-cli-binary-sha256-file` launcher-hash pin is retained only for\n33\tpre-ADR-182 tags; the live pin file is a comment-only tombstone, which\n34\tthat legacy path treats as \"no pin\" (skip).\n35\t\n36\t## parent_sha vs commit_sha (S104 redesign)\n37\t\n38\tThe legacy `--commit-sha` arg + verdict `commit_sha:` field bound the\n39\tverdict to a SHA the verdict commit itself produced — an unsolvable\n40\tself-reference (`pair-rail-verdict-vX.md` cannot declare its own commit\n41\tSHA because that SHA is only known AFTER the verdict file is committed).\n42\tThe v1.16.0 GA ceremony bridged this via `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1`\n43\ttransition mode, which silently disabled the bind.\n44\t\n45\t`parent_sha:` solves it cleanly. The verdict declares the commit it was\n46\tgenerated AGAINST (the parent of the verdict-file commit). That value is\n47\tknown when the verdict is authored (it's `git rev-parse HEAD` before the\n48\tverdict commit). Step 15 validates against `git log -n1 --format=%H --\n49\t<verdict-file>` parent, which is observable + immutable.\n50\t\n51\tBackward-compat: when only `commit_sha:` (legacy) is present and\n52\t`--parent-sha` is empty, the bind is skipped with an ADVISORY (matches\n53\tprior CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1 behavior). Legacy verdicts for\n54\talready-shipped tags (v1.16.0 etc.) keep their existing semantics; new\n55\tverdicts use `parent_sha:`.\n56\t\n57\t## Exit codes\n58\t\n59\t- 0: verdict valid; release proceeds.\n60\t- 1: infra error (file missing / unparseable / etc.); release.yml\n61\t     decides based on CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL.\n62\t- 2: VERDICT_EXPIRED — distinct from infra-error per R1 S-QA-Unseen-2.\n63\t     Release.yml can route this to a \"verdict regen\" branch.\n64\t- 3: VERDICT_INVALID — decision not authorizing (PLAN-177 W0.1) /\n65\t     non-canonical top-level key syntax, i.e. a spelling this reader and\n66\t     the local tag guard resolve differently (PLAN-177 t2) /\n67\t     release_tag mismatch / parent_sha mismatch / inputs_hash mismatch /\n68\t     pin mismatch / signature missing. Release MUST stop here.\n69\t\n70\tstdlib only. Python ≥3.9.\n71\t\"\"\"\n72\t\n73\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n74\t\n75\timport argparse\n76\timport hashlib\n77\timport json\n78\timport re\n79\timport subprocess\n80\timport sys\n81\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n82\tfrom pathlib import Path\n83\tfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n84\t\n85\t_REPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n86\t_HOOKS_DIR = _REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"hooks\"\n87\tsys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR)) if str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path else None\n88\tfrom _lib import cli_currency  # noqa: E402\n89\t\n90\tEXIT_OK = 0\n91\tEXIT_INFRA_ERROR = 1\n92\tEXIT_VERDICT_EXPIRED = 2\n93\tEXIT_VERDICT_INVALID = 3\n94\t\n95\t# PLAN-177 W0.1 (P1-4). The decisions that AUTHORIZE a release. Every other\n96\t# value — NO-GO, absent, empty, malformed, or simply unknown — is\n97\t# non-authorizing and stops the release. Spelling is the template's\n98\t# (.claude/governance/pair-rail-verdict-template.md:\n99\t# `verdict: GO | NO-GO | GO-WITH-CONDITIONS`); membership is tested by EXACT\n100\t# equality on purpose — case folding or a substring/prefix rule would read"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44354e61-c2ec-4181-9296-3322c9641608","uuid":"9e4f04c0-83bd-4485-89db-713f25a9ee4c","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:11:58.410Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.github/scripts/validate-pair-rail-verdict.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"validate-pair-rail-verdict.py — PLAN-081 Phase 6 release.yml step 15.\n\nValidates a Pair-Rail verdict artifact (`.claude/governance/\npair-rail-verdict-<release-tag>.md`) per R1 S-Sec-3 replay defense +\nR1 S-Sec-4 inputs_hash determinism + R1 C5 Codex CLI pin enforcement\n+ R1 S-QA-Unseen-2 distinct VERDICT_EXPIRED exit code.\n\n## Usage\n\n    python3 .github/scripts/validate-pair-rail-verdict.py \\\\\n      --verdict-file .claude/governance/pair-rail-verdict-${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md \\\\\n      --parent-sha ${PARENT_SHA} \\\\\n      --release-tag ${GITHUB_REF_NAME} \\\\\n      --max-age-hours 24 \\\\\n      --recompute-inputs-hash \\\\\n      --codex-cli-pin-file .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt \\\\\n      --codex-pin-manifest-file .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin-manifest.json \\\\\n      --inputs-hash-paths-file .claude/governance/pair-rail-inputs-hash-manifest.txt\n\n## ADR-182 payload pin (PLAN-163 T5.2)\n\n`--codex-pin-manifest-file` enforces the payload pin: the verdict\nenvelope MUST declare `tool_versions.codex_target_triple` (the platform\ntriple of the run that generated the verdict) and\n`tool_versions.codex_payload_sha256` (sha256 of the NATIVE codex\npayload for that triple — NOT the npm JS launcher). The validator\ncompares the declared sha against\n`manifest.payloads[<triple>].sha256`. Fail-CLOSED: missing fields,\ntriple absent from the manifest, malformed entry, or sha mismatch →\nVERDICT_INVALID (3). Manifest file unreadable → infra (1). The legacy\n`--codex-cli-binary-sha256-file` launcher-hash pin is retained only for\npre-ADR-182 tags; the live pin file is a comment-only tombstone, which\nthat legacy path treats as \"no pin\" (skip).\n\n## parent_sha vs commit_sha (S104 redesign)\n\nThe legacy `--commit-sha` arg + verdict `commit_sha:` field bound the\nverdict to a SHA the verdict commit itself produced — an unsolvable\nself-reference (`pair-rail-verdict-vX.md` cannot declare its own commit\nSHA because that SHA is only known AFTER the verdict file is committed).\nThe v1.16.0 GA ceremony bridged this via `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1`\ntransition mode, which silently disabled the bind.\n\n`parent_sha:` solves it cleanly. The verdict declares the commit it was\ngenerated AGAINST (the parent of the verdict-file commit). That value is\nknown when the verdict is authored (it's `git rev-parse HEAD` before the\nverdict commit). Step 15 validates against `git log -n1 --format=%H --\n<verdict-file>` parent, which is observable + immutable.\n\nBackward-compat: when only `commit_sha:` (legacy) is present and\n`--parent-sha` is empty, the bind is skipped with an ADVISORY (matches\nprior CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1 behavior). Legacy verdicts for\nalready-shipped tags (v1.16.0 etc.) keep their existing semantics; new\nverdicts use `parent_sha:`.\n\n## Exit codes\n\n- 0: verdict valid; release proceeds.\n- 1: infra error (file missing / unparseable / etc.); release.yml\n     decides based on CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL.\n- 2: VERDICT_EXPIRED — distinct from infra-error per R1 S-QA-Unseen-2.\n     Release.yml can route this to a \"verdict regen\" branch.\n- 3: VERDICT_INVALID — decision not authorizing (PLAN-177 W0.1) /\n     non-canonical top-level key syntax, i.e. a spelling this reader and\n     the local tag guard resolve differently (PLAN-177 t2) /\n     release_tag mismatch / parent_sha mismatch / inputs_hash mismatch /\n     pin mismatch / signature missing. Release MUST stop here.\n\nstdlib only. Python ≥3.9.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\n_REPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n_HOOKS_DIR = _REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"hooks\"\nsys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR)) if str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path else None\nfrom _lib import cli_currency  # noqa: E402\n\nEXIT_OK = 0\nEXIT_INFRA_ERROR = 1\nEXIT_VERDICT_EXPIRED = 2\nEXIT_VERDICT_INVALID = 3\n\n# PLAN-177 W0.1 (P1-4). The decisions that AUTHORIZE a release. Every other\n# value — NO-GO, absent, empty, malformed, or simply unknown — is\n# non-authorizing and stops the release. Spelling is the template's\n# (.claude/governance/pair-rail-verdict-template.md:\n# `verdict: GO | NO-GO | GO-WITH-CONDITIONS`); membership is tested by EXACT\n# equality on purpose — case folding or a substring/prefix rule would read","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":799}}