r-rail on the 0.139 CLI surface. The binary-SHA pin\n# (codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt -> d3be844c...) remains the real supply-chain\n# gate; this semver range is the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message. Per\n# ADR-111 the 0.128->0.139 jump runs the locked-corpus catch_rate check\n# (Owner elected to RUN it this ceremony, not defer) — see PLAN-142 §4.\n#\n# PLAN-156 update (S269 2026-07-12, SENT-CX-PIN): widened upper bound to\n# <0.145.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.144.1 is in-range — the\n# bump that restores frontier-model access (GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra/Luna are\n# first-class from 0.143.0; 0.139 cannot run them). LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED\n# at >=0.128.0 (debate C10 / pair-rail R2: raising it would drop an\n# in-flight RC verdict out of range in release.yml step-15 and red-lock a\n# GA cut — widen-upper-only is the ONLY safe shape during any release\n# window; this bump was executed OUTSIDE an open release window).\n# Empirical base: PLAN-156/artifacts/characterization-grok-codex-S269.md\n# (0.144.1 flag surface verified — the 0.139 verified-compose\n# `exec --color never --sandbox <mode> -o <file> --output-schema --json -m`\n# is UNCHANGED; sandbox enum still read-only|workspace-write|\n# danger-full-access; reasoning-effort accepts max/xhigh client-side;\n# 0.144.0 open bugs #31873/#31860/#31826 triaged non-blocking, #31869\n# CLOSED upstream 2026-07-10). Locked-corpus catch_rate check: Owner\n# elects run-vs-defer at SENT-CX-PIN signing (S246 precedent: run it).\n#\n# PLAN-174 update (S318 2026-08-20, pack SENT-S318): widened upper bound to\n# <0.148.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.147.0 is in-range — the bump\n# that unblocks the PLAN-174 W2 wire (the pair-rail rounds since S317 already\n# ran on the 0.147.0 binary, advisory). LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0\n# (same widen-upper-only shape as S269: executed OUTSIDE any open release\n# window — GA v1.3.0 was cut 2026-08-17 and no rc is in flight). The ADR-182\n# payload manifest (codex-cli-pin-manifest.json, re-pinned in this same pack:\n# payload sha256 19c4f144... for 0.147.0/aarch64-apple-darwin, npm_integrity\n# recorded from the platform artifact) remains the real supply-chain gate;\n# this semver range stays the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message.\n# Locked-corpus catch_rate check (ADR-111 §2): Owner elects run-vs-defer at\n# pack signing, recorded in the SENT-S318 sentinel Scope.\n\n# PLAN-189 update (S352 2026-09-15): widened upper bound to <0.155.0 so the\n# Owner's installed codex-cli 0.154.0 is in-range. The rail was pinned at\n# 0.147.0 while the global CLI had moved SEVEN releases ahead, so every rail\n# round ran on a revisor older than the one the Owner uses interactively.\n# Per ADR-111 §pin-update-protocol this widening does NOT trigger a Phase\n# 4-bis re-run: no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken. DECLARED\n# CONSEQUENCE: this changes the INSTRUMENT — rail measurements taken before\n# and after this commit are NOT comparable (S352 rule: re-test on a new\n# generation, instrument intact). The 93/93/91 validity series measured in\n# S352 was taken under 0.147.0.\n\n# PLAN-189 update (S356 2026-09-18, pack codex-pin-0155): widened upper bound\n# to <0.156.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.155.0 is in-range. 0.155.0\n# was published to npm on 2026-09-17; with the ADR-182 exact-version payload\n# manifest the pair-rail went fail-CLOSED in this repo (`--verify-codex-pin`\n# -> mismatch payload_sha256_mismatch) until this re-pin. LOWER BOUND\n# UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0 (widen-upper-only, the only safe shape), executed\n# OUTSIDE any open release window: GA v1.4.0 was cut 2026-09-15 and\n# v1.4.1-rc.1 is cut only AFTER this commit. Per ADR-111\n# §pin-update-protocol this widening does NOT trigger a Phase 4-bis re-run:\n# no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken. DECLARED CONSEQUENCE\n# (same as S352): this changes the INSTRUMENT — rail measurements taken\n# before and after this commit are NOT comparable. The payload manifest\n# (re-pinned in this same pack: payload sha256 b0b14f9c... for\n# 0.155.0/aarch64-apple-darwin, npm_integrity recorded from the PLATFORM\n# artifact per ADR-182 §5 step 2) remains the real supply-chain gate; this\n# semver range stays the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message.\n# Doctrine (S355): the Codex CLI is a SHA-pinned substrate — every Codex\n# upgrade requires this re-pin BEFORE any release cut; never a casual\n# `npm update -g`.\n\n# PLAN-193 update (S357 2026-09-23, pack codex-pin-0156): widened upper bound\n# to <0.157.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.156.1 is in-range. 0.156.1\n# was published to npm on 2026-09-23 as a hotfix of 0.156.0 (never pinned\n# here). With the ADR-182 exact-version payload manifest, installing it before\n# this re-pin closes the pair-rail (measured 2026-09-23 against the Owner's\n# installed 0.156.1: `--verify-codex-pin` -> mismatch payload_sha256_mismatch),\n# so the ceremony refuses to sign unless the installed payload already hashes\n# to the sha256 pinned below. LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0\n# (widen-upper-only; raising it past 0.139.0 would put the Codex host-adapter\n# fixtures, recorded under codex-cli 0.139.0, out of range). Landed only AFTER\n# the v1.4.1 GA tag (the ceremony refuses otherwise): release.yml step 15\n# checks the GA verdict's codex_cli against this range and its\n# codex_payload_sha256 against the manifest of the TAGGED tree, and this file\n# is hashed into the verdict's inputs_hash. DECLARED EXCEPTION to the S355\n# doctrine above: the Owner installed 0.156.1 globally on 2026-09-23, before\n# the v1.4.1 GA cut, so for that one cut the letter of \"every Codex upgrade\n# requires this re-pin BEFORE any release cut\" is not met. What still holds:\n# the validator that step 15 runs accepts the GA verdict only if the\n# verdict DECLARES a codex_cli inside the tagged range and the payload sha256\n# of the tagged manifest (0.155.0) — a check of the declaration, not a hash of\n# the binary that produced the verdict — so before these bytes land no verdict\n# declaring 0.156.1 validates; step 15's optional mode\n# (CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1, a repository variable unset on\n# 2026-09-23) goes beyond tolerating a failed validation: it also skips a\n# missing verdict file and drops the parent-SHA bind; the delta+ancestry\n# gate that follows it fails closed in that mode. Landing\n# these bytes before the tag would instead break the GA's own step 15\n# (inputs_hash and payload pin both change under a verdict produced on\n# 0.155.0). Corpus rule: ADR-111 §2, restated as ADR-182 §5 step 5 (the\n# `§pin-update-protocol` label above names no heading in ADR-111) — a CLI\n# bump reopens the corpus only on a MEASURED catch_rate shift >5pp. No\n# locked-corpus run was taken for this bump (the runner's default corpus path\n# is absent from this repository and its per-fixture review is still a stub),\n# so the trigger is unevaluated, not passed. The ADR-161 per-bump checklist is\n# deferred to the substrate wave, as declared in S356 (which recorded the S352\n# re-pin as the same posture): it re-certifies Codex as a HOOK HOST, while\n# what forces this re-pin is Codex as the rail REVIEWER. DECLARED CONSEQUENCE\n# of that deferral: the installer's Codex-harness version-skew warning\n# (scripts/_codex_harness.sh) reads this same range, so widening it admits\n# 0.156.x as in-range for Codex as a hook host while the hook evidence stays\n# at 0.139.0 — a re-certification this deferral knowingly waives (every\n# widening since that reader landed, on 2026-07-10, had the same effect).\n# From 0.155.0 to 0.156.0 the exec crate's output-shape change is confined to\n# web-search items of the `codex exec --json` stream, which has no reader in\n# live code (the live rail runs `exec -o` without `--json`, and the one parser\n# of that stream in the tracked tree outside .claude/plans/ has no caller\n# outside tests; the ADR-161 live-fire procedures under .claude/plans/PLAN-155/\n# do read that stream, but items other than web search — the only kind the\n# change touches — and stay deferred with the checklist); from 0.156.0 to\n# 0.156.1 the exec crate is unchanged (same git tree at both tags)\n# and, outside tests, only the workspace version, the bundled model catalog\n# and two TUI source files change — upstream says that catalog also feeds the\n# sub-agent tool descriptions sent to the model.\n# DECLARED CONSEQUENCE (same as S352/S356): this changes the INSTRUMENT —\n# rail measurements taken before and after this commit are NOT comparable.\n# The payload manifest (re-pinned in this same pack: payload sha256\n# 0196e89f... for 0.156.1/aarch64-apple-darwin, npm_integrity recorded from\n# the PLATFORM artifact per ADR-182 §5 step 2) remains the real supply-chain\n# gate; this range is a version gate (the release.yml step-15 validator reads\n# it, among others), not a supply-chain gate.\n\n# re-pin update (2026-10-02, pack codex-pin-0160; generated by\n# .claude/scripts/re-pin-codex.py): package_version 0.156.1 -> 0.160.0.\n# Upper bound widened <0.157.0 -> <0.161.0; LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at\n# >=0.128.0 (widen-upper-only). The payload manifest is re-pinned in this\n# same pack: payload sha256 112fae7a... for 0.160.0/aarch64-apple-darwin,\n# npm_integrity from the PLATFORM artifact\n# @openai/codex@0.160.0-darwin-arm64 (ADR-182 §5 step 2).\n# Why now: Owner decision of 2026-10-02 (S362), recorded in PLAN-194 as plan\n# B (manual re-pin from the newest mold, ADR-182 §5): this re-pin is the\n# FIRST task of the v1.4.3 maintenance train. PLAN-194 pending decision 3\n# (how the automatic pin is packaged) was NOT taken, so the automatic Codex\n# pin (PLAN-194 W3) moves after v1.4.3 and its Security VETO stays raised;\n# until it lands, every Codex upgrade goes through a pack generated like\n# this one.\n# Release window: executed OUTSIDE any open release window. GA v1.4.2 was\n# cut on 2026-09-30 and no v1.4.3 tag exists; the ceremony refuses to run\n# unless the v1.4.2 tag is an ancestor of HEAD. Doctrine (S355) met: this\n# re-pin lands BEFORE the next release cut. Only the UPPER bound widens; the\n# lower bound stays where it was (widen-upper-only, the only safe shape).\n# The payload manifest remains the real supply-chain gate; this range is a\n# version gate.\n# Corpus rule: ADR-111 §2, restated as ADR-182 §5 step 5, reopens the corpus\n# only on a MEASURED catch_rate shift >5pp on the locked corpus. That\n# trigger is NOT EVALUABLE in this tree: no locked-corpus run exists for\n# this bump (the runner's default corpus path is absent from this repository\n# and its per-fixture review is still a stub), so it is unevaluated, not\n# passed.\n# The ADR-161 per-bump checklist is DEFERRED, as in S352, S356 and S357: it\n# re-certifies Codex as a HOOK HOST, while what forces this re-pin is Codex\n# as the rail REVIEWER. DECLARED CONSEQUENCE of that deferral, stated by\n# shape: every consumer that reads this range as a version gate admits\n# 0.160.x from this commit on, the installer's Codex-harness version-skew\n# check (scripts/_codex_harness.sh) among them, while the hook evidence it\n# names stays certified on 0.139.0.\n# DECLARED CONSEQUENCE (same as S352, S356 and S357): this changes the\n# INSTRUMENT. The rail reviewer becomes the 0.160.0 binary; rail\n# measurements taken before and after this commit are NOT comparable, and\n# the first rail round on 0.160.0 is a re-test. What the reviewer serves is\n# chosen by the Owner's Codex config, not by this pin: measured on\n# 2026-10-02 (S362 probe of 0.160.0 in a disposable npm prefix) as model\n# gpt-6-astra at reasoning effort xhigh. A change of that config changes the\n# instrument without touching these bytes.\n# Residual, by shape: the pin attests ONE executable, the\n# aarch64-apple-darwin payload at the manifest path. Every other executable\n# is outside the sha: the sibling executables the platform tarball carries\n# beside it, the payloads of the other npm platforms, and the launcher of\n# the main package (bin/codex.js). Same posture as every earlier generation,\n# not a regression of this pack.\n# Current compatibility floor (Onda6B): stable Codex CLI releases at or above\n# 0.128.0 are compatible version evidence. This unbounded range is not a\n# payload-hash attestation; codex-cli-pin-manifest.json remains that gate.\n>=0.128.0\n","numLines":200,"startLine":1,"totalLines":200}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01G7Yx5RfDAMyY7KM7XBKGy4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
