{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011XEfmGBEAYiiA38P7C3sfM","type":"tool_result","content":"720\t          VERDICT_FILE=\".claude/governance/pair-rail-verdict-${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\"\n721\t          if [ ! -f \"$VERDICT_FILE\" ]; then\n722\t            if [ \"${CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL:-0}\" = \"1\" ]; then\n723\t              echo \"::notice::no verdict file at $VERDICT_FILE; CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1 → skipping\"\n724\t              exit 0\n725\t            fi\n726\t            echo \"::error::verdict file missing at $VERDICT_FILE — step 15 blocks release\"\n727\t            exit 1\n728\t          fi\n729\t          # S104 redesign: resolve PARENT_SHA = parent of the verdict-file\n730\t          # commit. The tag commit (${GITHUB_SHA}) is what we're releasing,\n731\t          # and the verdict file at $VERDICT_FILE either:\n732\t          #   (a) was committed in the tag commit itself → parent = ${GITHUB_SHA}^\n733\t          #   (b) was committed earlier (multi-commit prep) → parent = git log of file\n734\t          # We use (b)'s general form: find the commit that introduced the\n735\t          # current verdict file, then take its parent. This handles both\n736\t          # single-commit-with-verdict and multi-commit-prep flows.\n737\t          VERDICT_FILE_COMMIT=$(git log -n1 --format=%H -- \"$VERDICT_FILE\")\n738\t          if [ -z \"$VERDICT_FILE_COMMIT\" ]; then\n739\t            echo \"::error::cannot resolve commit for $VERDICT_FILE — step 15 fails\"\n740\t            exit 1\n741\t          fi\n742\t          PARENT_SHA=$(git rev-parse \"${VERDICT_FILE_COMMIT}^\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"\")\n743\t          if [ -z \"$PARENT_SHA\" ]; then\n744\t            echo \"::error::cannot resolve parent of $VERDICT_FILE_COMMIT — step 15 fails\"\n745\t            exit 1\n746\t          fi\n747\t          echo \"::notice::S104 bind: VERDICT_FILE_COMMIT=$VERDICT_FILE_COMMIT, PARENT_SHA=$PARENT_SHA\"\n748\t          # When transition mode is on, allow parent_sha mismatch (skip bind)\n749\t          # by passing empty string. Default is hard-bind on PARENT_SHA.\n750\t          PARENT_SHA_ARG=\"$PARENT_SHA\"\n751\t          if [ \"${CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL:-0}\" = \"1\" ]; then\n752\t            PARENT_SHA_ARG=\"\"\n753\t          fi\n754\t          python3 .github/scripts/validate-pair-rail-verdict.py \\\n755\t            --verdict-file \"$VERDICT_FILE\" \\\n756\t            --parent-sha \"$PARENT_SHA_ARG\" \\\n757\t            --release-tag \"${GITHUB_REF_NAME}\" \\\n758\t            --max-age-hours 24 \\\n759\t            --recompute-inputs-hash \\\n760\t            --codex-cli-pin-file .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt \\\n761\t            --codex-cli-binary-sha256-file .claude/governance/codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt \\\n762\t            --codex-pin-manifest-file .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin-manifest.json \\\n763\t            --inputs-hash-paths-file .claude/governance/pair-rail-inputs-hash-manifest.txt\n764\t\n765\t      # ==========================================================\n766\t      # PLAN-166 W1-B — verdict delta + ancestry gate (F2 server side)\n767\t      # ==========================================================\n768\t      # Re-pass findings r15 + r17 + r18 (PLAN-166), debate r3 scoped VETO.\n769\t      #\n770\t      # WHY A SEPARATE STEP: the step-15 neighbourhood above carries two\n771\t      # escape hatches keyed to CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL —\n772\t      # `continue-on-error:` on the step itself, and an empty\n773\t      # `--parent-sha \"\"` bind (the validator only binds the field when\n774\t      # args.parent_sha is non-empty). Inheriting that neighbourhood would\n775\t      # inherit the switch. This step therefore:\n776\t      #   - carries NO continue-on-error;\n777\t      #   - FAILS CLOSED when CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1: in that\n778\t      #     mode step 15 skipped the parent_sha bind, so the anchor these\n779\t      #     asserts hang off was never validated — there is no transition\n780\t      #     mode here, by design;\n781\t      #   - re-derives and re-binds parent_sha ITSELF (non-empty, 40-hex,\n782\t      #     equal to the verdict's `parent_sha:` read with the SAME parser\n783\t      #     the local tag guard uses) — independent of step 15's outcome,\n784\t      #     which also closes the legacy commit_sha fallback (the\n785\t      #     validator downgrades a missing parent_sha to an ADVISORY when\n786\t      #     a legacy commit_sha is present; this step does not);\n787\t      #   - reuses .claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py for the\n788\t      #     delta decision — the module marks itself as the reference\n789\t      #     implementation; the semantics are NEVER re-implemented in\n790\t      #     bash (single source of the decision logic);\n791\t      #   - asserts ancestry on origin/main of BOTH the reviewed parent\n792\t      #     AND GITHUB_SHA itself (r18: parent-only lets the\n793\t      #     tag-without-push scenario — verdict V over parent P, tag\n794\t      #     pushed, V never reaches main — pass with P ancestral and V\n795\t      #     orphaned).\n796\t      #\n797\t      # THE INVARIANT (one sentence): nothing landed after what the\n798\t      # re-pass reviewed, other than the verdict for THIS tag and the\n799\t      # evidence it pins by name AND content (sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44354e61-c2ec-4181-9296-3322c9641608","uuid":"dca692ac-92ac-423e-aa99-bb3652d34342","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:12:27.394Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.github/workflows/release.yml","content":"          VERDICT_FILE=\".claude/governance/pair-rail-verdict-${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\"\n          if [ ! -f \"$VERDICT_FILE\" ]; then\n            if [ \"${CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL:-0}\" = \"1\" ]; then\n              echo \"::notice::no verdict file at $VERDICT_FILE; CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1 → skipping\"\n              exit 0\n            fi\n            echo \"::error::verdict file missing at $VERDICT_FILE — step 15 blocks release\"\n            exit 1\n          fi\n          # S104 redesign: resolve PARENT_SHA = parent of the verdict-file\n          # commit. The tag commit (${GITHUB_SHA}) is what we're releasing,\n          # and the verdict file at $VERDICT_FILE either:\n          #   (a) was committed in the tag commit itself → parent = ${GITHUB_SHA}^\n          #   (b) was committed earlier (multi-commit prep) → parent = git log of file\n          # We use (b)'s general form: find the commit that introduced the\n          # current verdict file, then take its parent. This handles both\n          # single-commit-with-verdict and multi-commit-prep flows.\n          VERDICT_FILE_COMMIT=$(git log -n1 --format=%H -- \"$VERDICT_FILE\")\n          if [ -z \"$VERDICT_FILE_COMMIT\" ]; then\n            echo \"::error::cannot resolve commit for $VERDICT_FILE — step 15 fails\"\n            exit 1\n          fi\n          PARENT_SHA=$(git rev-parse \"${VERDICT_FILE_COMMIT}^\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"\")\n          if [ -z \"$PARENT_SHA\" ]; then\n            echo \"::error::cannot resolve parent of $VERDICT_FILE_COMMIT — step 15 fails\"\n            exit 1\n          fi\n          echo \"::notice::S104 bind: VERDICT_FILE_COMMIT=$VERDICT_FILE_COMMIT, PARENT_SHA=$PARENT_SHA\"\n          # When transition mode is on, allow parent_sha mismatch (skip bind)\n          # by passing empty string. Default is hard-bind on PARENT_SHA.\n          PARENT_SHA_ARG=\"$PARENT_SHA\"\n          if [ \"${CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL:-0}\" = \"1\" ]; then\n            PARENT_SHA_ARG=\"\"\n          fi\n          python3 .github/scripts/validate-pair-rail-verdict.py \\\n            --verdict-file \"$VERDICT_FILE\" \\\n            --parent-sha \"$PARENT_SHA_ARG\" \\\n            --release-tag \"${GITHUB_REF_NAME}\" \\\n            --max-age-hours 24 \\\n            --recompute-inputs-hash \\\n            --codex-cli-pin-file .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt \\\n            --codex-cli-binary-sha256-file .claude/governance/codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt \\\n            --codex-pin-manifest-file .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin-manifest.json \\\n            --inputs-hash-paths-file .claude/governance/pair-rail-inputs-hash-manifest.txt\n\n      # ==========================================================\n      # PLAN-166 W1-B — verdict delta + ancestry gate (F2 server side)\n      # ==========================================================\n      # Re-pass findings r15 + r17 + r18 (PLAN-166), debate r3 scoped VETO.\n      #\n      # WHY A SEPARATE STEP: the step-15 neighbourhood above carries two\n      # escape hatches keyed to CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL —\n      # `continue-on-error:` on the step itself, and an empty\n      # `--parent-sha \"\"` bind (the validator only binds the field when\n      # args.parent_sha is non-empty). Inheriting that neighbourhood would\n      # inherit the switch. This step therefore:\n      #   - carries NO continue-on-error;\n      #   - FAILS CLOSED when CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1: in that\n      #     mode step 15 skipped the parent_sha bind, so the anchor these\n      #     asserts hang off was never validated — there is no transition\n      #     mode here, by design;\n      #   - re-derives and re-binds parent_sha ITSELF (non-empty, 40-hex,\n      #     equal to the verdict's `parent_sha:` read with the SAME parser\n      #     the local tag guard uses) — independent of step 15's outcome,\n      #     which also closes the legacy commit_sha fallback (the\n      #     validator downgrades a missing parent_sha to an ADVISORY when\n      #     a legacy commit_sha is present; this step does not);\n      #   - reuses .claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py for the\n      #     delta decision — the module marks itself as the reference\n      #     implementation; the semantics are NEVER re-implemented in\n      #     bash (single source of the decision logic);\n      #   - asserts ancestry on origin/main of BOTH the reviewed parent\n      #     AND GITHUB_SHA itself (r18: parent-only lets the\n      #     tag-without-push scenario — verdict V over parent P, tag\n      #     pushed, V never reaches main — pass with P ancestral and V\n      #     orphaned).\n      #\n      # THE INVARIANT (one sentence): nothing landed after what the\n      # re-pass reviewed, other than the verdict for THIS tag and the\n      # evidence it pins by name AND content (sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256","numLines":80,"startLine":720,"totalLines":1000}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011XEfmGBEAYiiA38P7C3sfM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
