{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X7jbPdej797Rq9SeMZzjui","type":"tool_result","content":"16:#   --stack <name>                 Stack-specific hooks to merge into settings.json\n138:#   4. Produces .claude/settings.json from templates/settings/settings.base.json\n142:#      baseline into the permissions.deny of a settings.json THIS run\n147:#      check_bash_safety.py's parse gate. Skipped when settings.json\n1140:# mcp__codex__codex-reply matchers in settings.json). install_template is\n1189:  rels=\".claude/settings.json\n1724:# policy files + fixtures + drift-manifest. settings.json keeps pointing\n1726:# YAML path by editing settings.json post-install after reviewing the\n2279:echo \"==> Building settings.json\"\n2282:SETTINGS_DST=\"$TARGET/.claude/settings.json\"\n2292:# symlinks. A DANGLING link at .claude/settings.json therefore answered\n2297:if _dst_refuses \".claude/settings.json\"; then\n2301:# PLAN-153 Wave E item 3: remember whether settings.json pre-existed so the\n2321:      echo \"    (dry-run) EXISTS (would skip settings.json)\"\n2325:      echo \"    (dry-run) would COPY settings.base.json -> .claude/settings.json (base only)\"\n2334:      echo \"    (dry-run) would MERGE settings.base.json + settings.stack.$STACK.json -> .claude/settings.json\"\n2346:    echo \"    EXISTS (skipping settings.json — edit manually if you want to re-build)\"\n2355:    echo \"    COPIED: settings.base.json -> .claude/settings.json (base only, no stack hooks)\"\n2369:    # settings.json with the hook fragment but NO `.sandbox` /\n2387:    echo \"    MERGED: settings.base.json + settings.stack.$STACK.json -> .claude/settings.json\"\n2417:# Injects a small permissions.deny baseline into the settings.json THIS\n2436:# Idempotency: runs ONLY when this run created settings.json\n2437:# (SETTINGS_PRE_EXISTING=0). Re-running install skips settings.json\n2444:# the just-copied settings.json untouched.\n2449:# permissions.defaultMode = DEFAULT_MODE_BASELINE when the settings.json this\n2455:# own) is kept as-is, and a pre-existing settings.json is never touched (see\n2502:      echo \"    (dry-run) settings.json pre-existed — would NOT touch deny baseline + defaultMode\"\n2504:      echo \"    (dry-run) would MERGE ${#DENY_BASELINE_ENTRIES[@]} deny-baseline entries (+ permissions.defaultMode \\\"$DEFAULT_MODE_BASELINE\\\" if absent) into .claude/settings.json\"\n2510:    echo \"    SKIP: deny baseline + defaultMode — settings.json pre-existed this run (add them manually if wanted — docs/deny-baseline.md)\"\n2541:      echo \"    MERGED: ${#DENY_BASELINE_ENTRIES[@]}-entry coarse deny baseline (+ permissions.defaultMode if absent) -> .claude/settings.json (docs/deny-baseline.md)\"\n2545:    echo \"    WARNING: jq merge of the deny baseline failed — settings.json left untouched.\" >&2\n2566:      echo \"    MERGED: ${#DENY_BASELINE_ENTRIES[@]}-entry coarse deny baseline (+ permissions.defaultMode if absent) -> .claude/settings.json (python3; docs/deny-baseline.md)\"\n2570:    echo \"    WARNING: python3 merge of the deny baseline failed — settings.json left untouched.\" >&2\n2959:  #   - .claude/settings.json          (user-edited hook registry)\n3737:# hooks — the legacy .claude/settings.json is the armed surface, OQ1).\n3875:# check. /doctor validates settings.json / hooks / MCP wiring from inside the\n3880:echo \"    4. Run \\`claude\\` and type \\`/doctor\\` once: confirm settings.json parses,\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44354e61-c2ec-4181-9296-3322c9641608","uuid":"a4f19bbc-3c53-468a-b33b-4cc36fd8779c","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:12:49.005Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"16:#   --stack <name>                 Stack-specific hooks to merge into settings.json\n138:#   4. Produces .claude/settings.json from templates/settings/settings.base.json\n142:#      baseline into the permissions.deny of a settings.json THIS run\n147:#      check_bash