s; check_bash_safety.py is 42 lines.\\n  - The six new top-level script helpers exist.\\n  - templates/settings, install.sh and upgrade.sh are absent from scope-rc1.txt, which supports \\\"unchanged since v1.4.3-rc.1\\\".\\n  - install.sh builds .claude/settings.json only from templates (install.sh:2279-2387), so 3650 and claudeMdExcludes do not reach installs.\\n  - The claudeMdExcludes glob has no unmodelled syntax. Under claude_md_excludes._segments_match it matches the root CLAUDE.md only if the checkout itself sits under .claude/plans/**/staged*/.\\n\\nADOPTER BLAST RADIUS, FAIL DIRECTION, MOVED CODE, PYTHON\\n- No silent model change. tier_policy_cli.loader is consumed only by tier_policy_cli/cli.py. The runtime hook path uses _lib/tier_policy, a closed MODEL_ID enum that this payload does not touch. apply.py:401 still requires exact VALID_MODEL_IDS membership before rewriting any agent `model:` line, so a family id admitted by loader.py:251 or learn.py:462 is never written.\\n- Fail direction is correct:\\n  - The validator exits 3 (fails closed) on an unparseable pin line (:353-358, :594), a malformed verdict payload sha (:748-751) or a non-stable manifest package_version (:715).\\n  - A failed `_lib` import crashes with exit 1 (INFRA), and the PLAN-166 delta gate still fails closed in optional mode.\\n  - validate-governance.sh:721 counts an ERROR when python3 or model_currency.py is missing.\\n  - _types.py:27-36 falls back to the exact list on ImportError.\\n- Shadowing:\\n  - Running `python3 .claude/hooks/_lib/model_currency.py` puts _lib/ at sys.path[0]. No _lib/*.py name collides with a stdlib module that model_currency or the interpreter needs.\\n  - The new sys.path.insert(0, .claude/hooks) in _types.py:24-26 and validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:85-88 shadows nothing. No hook file has a stdlib name or the name of a module tier_policy_cli imports (apply, learn, loader, _types, _constants).\\n- Removed validator names (parse_semver, semver_in_range) have no callers outside tests.\\n- MODEL_ID is now `str`. It has no runtime consumer, and the VALID_MODEL_IDS reorder affects no indexer.\\n- Everything is stdlib only and safe on Python 3.9.\\n\\nP0: none.\\n\\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): no new P1.\\n- Carried P1, still open on this code: lane note claude-p32. validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:85-88 and :768-772 and validate-governance.sh:721 hand ADR-192 gate decisions to _lib/cli_currency.py and _lib/model_currency.py. Neither is in gate-scripts-manifest.txt, and cli_currency.py is not in pair-rail-inputs-hash-manifest.txt. Nothing between the rc tag and the GA candidate changed this.\\n\\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\\n1. NEW. validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:21-34, release.yml:694-696 and docs/CROSS-LLM-THREAT-MODEL.md:350 still say that a payload sha mismatch means VERDICT_INVALID, with the payload sha equal to the manifest.\\n   - Failure scenario: after this delta, that is false for any declared codex_cli newer than the manifest version (version_comparison != 0 and newer_floor >= 0). A reader of step 15 or the threat model believes the hash gate is unconditional. The CHANGELOG declares the gate change and the stale operating contract, but not these three texts.\\n   - Fix: amend all three to state the version-floor exemption.\\n2. NEW. tier_policy_cli/cli.py:349-351 says VALID_MODEL_IDS has \\\"claude-fable-5 [as] its first entry\\\". _types.py:55-57 now puts claude-opus-4-8 first. Also _types.py:8,143 and tier_policy_cli/__init__.py:17 still say \\\"MODEL_ID Literal\\\".\\n   - Fix: update the comments.\\n3. Carried, latent. validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:772 `version_comparison in (None, 0)` also exempts a version OLDER than the manifest when it is at or above the floor.\\n   - Status: harmless while package_version == CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR == 0.160.0 (codex-cli-pin-manifest.json:3). It becomes live at the next re-pin. The INFO text at :783 (\\\"newer than the payload manifest\\\") would then be false.\\n   - Fix: `exact_payload_pin = version_comparison is None or version_comparison <= 0 or newer_floor is None or newer_floor < 0`.\\n4. Carried. scripts/_codex_harness.sh:46,294,373,461 put CODEX_VERIFIED_VERSION=0.160.0 into two places:\\n   - the requirements.toml that adopters commit (\\\"Verified against codex-cli 0.160.0\\\");\\n   - the arming-check skew text (\\\"certified on 0.160.0\\\").\\n   The hook fixtures date from 0.139.0. Also, the CHANGELOG calls it the helper \\\"that install.sh sources\\\", but upgrade.sh sources it too (header :8).\\n   - Fix: add a separate CODEX_FIXTURE_VERSION=0.139.0 for the certification wording.\\n5. Carried. learn.py:462 and loader.py:251 admit families, while apply.py:401 and cli.py:332-341 keep the exact list.\\n   - Effect: a learned or loaded family tier can never be applied or owner-signed. learn._tier_rank:547-564 ranks such ids -1, which mislabels the direction.\\n   - This fails safe. The CHANGELOG names the loader but not the learner.\\n   - Fix: use one predicate across learn, load, sign and apply.\\n6. Carried. check-subprocess-tests.py:16 reaches installs, but its subprocess-test-baseline.json does not. In an install it exits 2. It is a maintainer tool.\\n   - Fix: ship the baseline or exclude the tool from installs.\\n7. Carried. validate-governance.sh:701-710: the comment still describes a closed literal list.\\n8. Carried. SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:484 still says \\\"all four learning-loop rails\\\"; there are now five.\\n9. Carried. docs/DISASTER-RECOVERY.md:79-83 omits that an ABSENT counter exits 0 with only a warning (audit-verify-chain.py:44,582).\\n   - Failure scenario: in a truncated-tail investigation, a deleted sidecar reads as a pass.\\n   - Fix: state the absent case.\\n10. Carried. The two pin-file readers disagree on which data line they read:\\n    - parse_pin_range (validator :349-358) reads the FIRST data line and fails on a mismatch;\\n    - _codex_harness.sh:53 reads the LAST one.\\n    A second range line would make them disagree.\\n    - Fix: refuse more than one data line in both.\\n11. NEW, cosmetic. The heading \\\"[1.4.4] - 2026-11-03\\\" predates the review stamps (2026-11-09) and the GA cut. Keep-a-Changelog headings carry the release date.\\n\\nNOT VERIFIABLE HERE\\n- Whether gate-scripts-manifest.txt holds the current hashes of the edited validate-pair-rail-verdict.py and validate-governance.sh. I had no hashing tool and the copy is redacted. A stale hash fails release.yml closed, with no adopter impact.\\n- The git history between the rc tag and the GA candidate. Only the path and hunk match above was checkable.\",\"decision\":\"GO-WITH-CONDITIONS\",\"sentence\":\"All declared conditions this payload touches hold against the tree, there is no P0 and no new P1, and nothing reaches an adopter as a silent model change or a fail-direction inversion; the release still depends on the declared conditions, because the carried P1 (claude-p32) remains open on this same code.\"}","structured_output":{"report":"SCOPE (payload 34/34). The changed files are: subprocess-test-baseline.json (new), tier_policy_cli/{_types,learn,loader}.py, validate-governance.sh, .claude/settings.json, the PR template, validate-pair-rail-verdict.py, coverage.yml, validate.yml, CHANGELOG [1.4.4], INSTALL.md, Makefile, the READMEs, docs/*, the SBOM/SECURITY/VERSIONING stamps, SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md, VERSION, npm/package.json, pyproject.toml, scripts/_codex_harness.sh and scripts/install-npm.sh.\n\nThis list matches .claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/paths-rc1-32.txt line for line. Sampled hunks are identical in diff-rc1-32.patch: the CHANGELOG [1.4.4] span, exact_payload_pin, CODEX_VERIFIED_VERSION, cleanupPeriodDays 3650 and the install-npm.sh unpacking. That fits the GA-only claim that no in-scope byte changed after the rc tag.\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS CHECKED AGAINST THE TREE (none found false)\n- Condition 5: coverage.yml timeout-minutes is 50.\n- Condition 9: model_currency.py:7-16 (_RETIRED = {claude-o